From 0bcc77c1fd593ac981aa99a1c427503aee2f6cc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:01:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] draw: allocate a layer larger than the whole budget when
 none is held

lv_draw_layer_alloc_buf() refuses a layer whenever the layers already
allocated plus the new one would exceed LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY, so the
draw unit leaves the task for later, expecting another layer to finish
and free memory. A layer that alone is larger than the budget can never
fit. With no other layer holding memory nothing will ever be freed, the
layer's tasks are never taken, and lv_refr keeps dispatching forever:
the UI hangs with the process alive.

AERA hits this with LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY 4 MiB once transforms go
through layers: on an adaptive-resolution device the logical screen is
1440x2696, and a Recents card shrunk on press needs a transform layer of
its on-screen size (8 MiB or more). Tapping it hung recovery.

Allocate such a layer when no other layer holds memory; the budget still
limits layers that are rendered at the same time. Also close the
profiler section on that early return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
---
 src/draw/lv_draw.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/draw/lv_draw.c b/src/draw/lv_draw.c
index dc4ce2219..c97267049 100644
--- a/src/draw/lv_draw.c
+++ b/src/draw/lv_draw.c
@@ -493,9 +493,13 @@ void * lv_draw_layer_alloc_buf(lv_layer_t * layer)
 
 #if LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY > 0
     /* Do not allocate the layer if the sum of allocated layer sizes
-     * will exceed `LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY` */
-    if((_draw_info.used_memory_for_layers + layer_size_byte) > LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY) {
+     * will exceed `LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY`. A layer that is larger than the
+     * whole budget is still allocated when no other layer holds memory:
+     * waiting would never free enough for it, and rendering would wait forever. */
+    if(_draw_info.used_memory_for_layers > 0 &&
+       (_draw_info.used_memory_for_layers + layer_size_byte) > LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY) {
         LV_LOG_WARN("LV_DRAW_LAYER_MAX_MEMORY was reached when allocating the layer.");
+        LV_PROFILER_DRAW_END;
         return NULL;
     }
 #endif
